{"question_id": "q02", "model": "nvidia/nemotron-3.5-lightning:free", "set_version": 1, "answer_text": "ToolBench measures whether a model selects the correct tool and fills its argument schema (argument correctness), as well as the order of function calls. [S1]", "sources": [{"alias": "S1", "external_id": "ag-02", "tier": "vetted_preprint"}, {"alias": "S2", "external_id": "ag-11", "tier": "lab_blog"}, {"alias": "S3", "external_id": "dc-01", "tier": "peer_reviewed"}, {"alias": "S4", "external_id": "ag-18", "tier": "lab_blog"}, {"alias": "S5", "external_id": "ag-08", "tier": "lab_blog"}, {"alias": "S6", "external_id": "ag-05", "tier": "peer_reviewed"}, {"alias": "S7", "external_id": "ml-02", "tier": "vetted_preprint"}, {"alias": "S8", "external_id": "ag-01", "tier": "peer_reviewed"}], "tools": ["search_corpus"], "tokens": 2953, "provider_error": false}
{"question_id": "q03", "model": "nvidia/nemotron-3.5-lightning:free", "set_version": 1, "answer_text": "In the multi\u2011agent coordination framework **AgentCoord**, a dispatcher is responsible for assigning subtasks to distinct workers and actively avoids duplicated effort by ensuring each task is allocated only once [S1]. This explicit task\u2011allocation and coordination mechanism is what prevents multiple assistants from performing the same subtask.", "sources": [{"alias": "S1", "external_id": "ag-03", "tier": "peer_reviewed"}, {"alias": "S2", "external_id": "ag-12", "tier": "peer_reviewed"}, {"alias": "S3", "external_id": "ag-05", "tier": "peer_reviewed"}, {"alias": "S4", "external_id": "ag-11", "tier": "lab_blog"}, {"alias": "S5", "external_id": "ag-04", "tier": "vetted_preprint"}, {"alias": "S6", "external_id": "ml-02", "tier": "vetted_preprint"}, {"alias": "S7", "external_id": "ag-02", "tier": "vetted_preprint"}, {"alias": "S8", "external_id": "ag-18", "tier": "lab_blog"}], "tools": ["search_corpus", "get_item"], "tokens": 5115, "provider_error": false}
{"question_id": "q04", "model": "nvidia/nemotron-3.5-lightning:free", "set_version": 1, "answer_text": "An assistant can recall old notes without expanding the model\u2019s context window by **storing the notes in an external memory store and paging only the relevant snippets into the limited context at query time**\u202f[S1].  \nA typical approach works like this:\n\n1. **Memory store** \u2013 all past conversations or notes are kept in a persistent store (e.g., a vector database or a relational log).  \n2. **Ranking/retrieval** \u2013 when a question about old notes arises, a retrieval pipeline fetches the most relevant passages. Hybrid search can combine keyword and semantic matching to surface the right snippets\u202f[S2].  \n3. **Paging into context** \u2013 only the top\u2011ranked passages are inserted into the model\u2019s limited context window, keeping the total token count small while still giving the model the needed information.  \n4. **Efficient long\u2011range modelling** \u2013 alternatives such as state\u2011space models can scan a sequence with a fixed\u2011size memory, offering linear cost and strong long\u2011range recall\u202f[S8].\n\nIn short, the key ideas are **external memory + ranked retrieval + selective paging**, as described in the MemGPT work\u202f[S1] and supported by retrieval\u2011pipeline techniques\u202f[S2] and efficient sequence models\u202f[S8].", "sources": [{"alias": "S1", "external_id": "ag-04", "tier": "vetted_preprint"}, {"alias": "S2", "external_id": "ag-17", "tier": "vetted_preprint"}, {"alias": "S3", "external_id": "dec-01", "tier": "lab_blog"}, {"alias": "S4", "external_id": "ag-16", "tier": "peer_reviewed"}, {"alias": "S5", "external_id": "nm-03", "tier": "lab_blog"}, {"alias": "S6", "external_id": "dec-04", "tier": "lab_blog"}, {"alias": "S7", "external_id": "dec-05", "tier": "vetted_preprint"}, {"alias": "S8", "external_id": "ml-02", "tier": "vetted_preprint"}], "tools": ["search_corpus", "search_corpus"], "tokens": 4627, "provider_error": false}
{"question_id": "q05", "model": "nvidia/nemotron-3.5-lightning:free", "set_version": 1, "answer_text": "A sandbox limits untrusted code by restricting the program\u2019s read/write capabilities and by assigning permissions that control which runtime features the code may use; container isolation further contains any misbehaving process\u202f[S1].", "sources": [{"alias": "S1", "external_id": "ag-06", "tier": "lab_blog"}, {"alias": "S2", "external_id": "ag-01", "tier": "peer_reviewed"}, {"alias": "S3", "external_id": "ag-16", "tier": "peer_reviewed"}, {"alias": "S4", "external_id": "ml-03", "tier": "peer_reviewed"}, {"alias": "S5", "external_id": "af-03", "tier": "peer_reviewed"}, {"alias": "S6", "external_id": "ag-14", "tier": "peer_reviewed"}, {"alias": "S7", "external_id": "ag-17", "tier": "vetted_preprint"}, {"alias": "S8", "external_id": "ag-10", "tier": "vetted_preprint"}], "tools": ["search_corpus"], "tokens": 3042, "provider_error": false}
{"question_id": "q06", "model": "nvidia/nemotron-3.5-lightning:free", "set_version": 1, "answer_text": "Planning a sequence of steps before taking any action helps break a goal into ordered, manageable actions and allows the planner to revise the plan if a step fails\u202f[S1]. After each step, a **verifier** checks the outcome to confirm that the action produced the expected result\u202f[S1].", "sources": [{"alias": "S1", "external_id": "ag-09", "tier": "peer_reviewed"}, {"alias": "S2", "external_id": "ag-18", "tier": "lab_blog"}, {"alias": "S3", "external_id": "ag-03", "tier": "peer_reviewed"}, {"alias": "S4", "external_id": "dc-02", "tier": "vetted_preprint"}, {"alias": "S5", "external_id": "ag-14", "tier": "peer_reviewed"}, {"alias": "S6", "external_id": "ag-12", "tier": "peer_reviewed"}, {"alias": "S7", "external_id": "dec-02", "tier": "vetted_preprint"}, {"alias": "S8", "external_id": "dec-05", "tier": "vetted_preprint"}], "tools": ["search_corpus", "search_corpus"], "tokens": 4436, "provider_error": false}
{"question_id": "q07", "model": "nvidia/nemotron-3.5-lightning:free", "set_version": 1, "answer_text": "Self\u2011correction produces gains when the system\u2019s critic is grounded in a **checkable signal** \u2014 i.e., the feedback must be verifiable against external evidence or a task\u2011specific reward [S1].", "sources": [{"alias": "S1", "external_id": "ag-10", "tier": "vetted_preprint"}, {"alias": "S2", "external_id": "ag-02", "tier": "vetted_preprint"}, {"alias": "S3", "external_id": "dc-02", "tier": "vetted_preprint"}, {"alias": "S4", "external_id": "dec-04", "tier": "lab_blog"}, {"alias": "S5", "external_id": "af-04", "tier": "vetted_preprint"}, {"alias": "S6", "external_id": "ag-05", "tier": "peer_reviewed"}, {"alias": "S7", "external_id": "ag-16", "tier": "peer_reviewed"}, {"alias": "S8", "external_id": "ag-07", "tier": "vetted_preprint"}, {"alias": "S9", "external_id": "dec-02", "tier": "vetted_preprint"}], "tools": ["search_corpus", "search_corpus", "get_item"], "tokens": 7816, "provider_error": false}
{"question_id": "q08", "model": "nvidia/nemotron-3.5-lightning:free", "set_version": 1, "answer_text": "A strict spending limit is kept from being exceeded primarily by a **token budget** that halts further model calls once the allotted cap is reached\u202f[S1]. In addition, tools such as **LedgerGuard** actively flag runs that surpass their budget, providing an early\u2011warning or corrective mechanism\u202f[S5].", "sources": [{"alias": "S1", "external_id": "ag-11", "tier": "lab_blog"}, {"alias": "S2", "external_id": "ag-14", "tier": "peer_reviewed"}, {"alias": "S3", "external_id": "ag-06", "tier": "lab_blog"}, {"alias": "S4", "external_id": "ag-01", "tier": "peer_reviewed"}, {"alias": "S5", "external_id": "dc-03", "tier": "lab_blog"}, {"alias": "S6", "external_id": "ag-15", "tier": "lab_blog"}, {"alias": "S7", "external_id": "ag-13", "tier": "vetted_preprint"}, {"alias": "S8", "external_id": "ag-17", "tier": "vetted_preprint"}], "tools": ["search_corpus", "search_corpus"], "tokens": 4230, "provider_error": false}
{"question_id": "q09", "model": "nvidia/nemotron-3.5-lightning:free", "set_version": 1, "answer_text": "Before a dangerous (risky) step runs in a workflow, a human-in-the-loop review pauses the process. The reviewer sees the proposed action and its supporting evidence, and the workflow resumes only after approval [S2].", "sources": [{"alias": "S1", "external_id": "ag-09", "tier": "peer_reviewed"}, {"alias": "S2", "external_id": "ag-12", "tier": "peer_reviewed"}, {"alias": "S3", "external_id": "dc-02", "tier": "vetted_preprint"}, {"alias": "S4", "external_id": "ag-14", "tier": "peer_reviewed"}, {"alias": "S5", "external_id": "ag-13", "tier": "vetted_preprint"}, {"alias": "S6", "external_id": "ag-11", "tier": "lab_blog"}, {"alias": "S7", "external_id": "ml-02", "tier": "vetted_preprint"}, {"alias": "S8", "external_id": "ag-01", "tier": "peer_reviewed"}, {"alias": "S9", "external_id": "ml-01", "tier": "peer_reviewed"}, {"alias": "S10", "external_id": "dc-03", "tier": "lab_blog"}], "tools": ["search_corpus", "get_item", "search_corpus", "search_corpus"], "tokens": 12020, "provider_error": false}
