{"question_id": "q13", "model": "nvidia/nemotron-3.5-lightning:free", "set_version": 1, "answer_text": "According to the vetted preprint S1, spoofed speech detection must generalise to voices it has never been trained on, and the use of front-end features together with augmentation reduces the model's reliance on a \"speaker shortcut,\" thereby improving generalisation to unseen speakers [S1]. This indicates that effective generalisation is achieved by limiting dependency on speaker-specific cues and instead focusing on synthesis-related artifacts. [S1 tier: vetted_preprint]", "sources": [{"alias": "S1", "external_id": "af-04", "tier": "vetted_preprint"}, {"alias": "S2", "external_id": "af-01", "tier": "peer_reviewed"}, {"alias": "S3", "external_id": "ml-04", "tier": "vetted_preprint"}, {"alias": "S4", "external_id": "ag-12", "tier": "peer_reviewed"}, {"alias": "S5", "external_id": "ag-09", "tier": "peer_reviewed"}, {"alias": "S6", "external_id": "dc-03", "tier": "lab_blog"}, {"alias": "S7", "external_id": "ag-04", "tier": "vetted_preprint"}, {"alias": "S8", "external_id": "ml-06", "tier": "peer_reviewed"}, {"alias": "S9", "external_id": "ag-17", "tier": "vetted_preprint"}, {"alias": "S10", "external_id": "ag-18", "tier": "lab_blog"}, {"alias": "S11", "external_id": "ag-15", "tier": "lab_blog"}], "tools": ["search_corpus", "get_item", "search_corpus", "search_corpus"], "tokens": 11053, "provider_error": false}
{"question_id": "q14", "model": "nvidia/nemotron-3.5-lightning:free", "set_version": 1, "answer_text": "Sparse attention reduces the quadratic\u202fO(N\u00b2) cost of full self\u2011attention by selecting only a subset of key positions for each query, so the computation scales sub\u2011quadratically [S1] (peer\u2011reviewed). State\u2011space models replace the quadratic attention mechanism with a recurrence over a fixed\u2011size memory, achieving linear\u202fO(N) cost while still modeling long\u2011range dependencies [S2] (vetted preprint).", "sources": [{"alias": "S1", "external_id": "ml-01", "tier": "peer_reviewed"}, {"alias": "S2", "external_id": "ml-02", "tier": "vetted_preprint"}, {"alias": "S3", "external_id": "dec-05", "tier": "vetted_preprint"}, {"alias": "S4", "external_id": "ag-11", "tier": "lab_blog"}, {"alias": "S5", "external_id": "ag-07", "tier": "vetted_preprint"}, {"alias": "S6", "external_id": "dc-03", "tier": "lab_blog"}, {"alias": "S7", "external_id": "af-04", "tier": "vetted_preprint"}, {"alias": "S8", "external_id": "af-05", "tier": "lab_blog"}], "tools": ["search_corpus", "get_item", "get_item"], "tokens": 6978, "provider_error": false}
{"question_id": "q15", "model": "nvidia/nemotron-3.5-lightning:free", "set_version": 1, "answer_text": "Based on the corpus, here's how each mechanism changes a transformer:\n\n**Mixture-of-experts routing**  \n- Activates only a few feed-forward blocks per token, rather than all blocks [S1].  \n- A router balances load and quality, directing tokens to expert modules [S1].  \n- Can be budget\u2011aware: easy requests go to a cheap model, hard ones to a stronger model, and a token budget stops spending once a run reaches its cap [S3].  \n- Sparse routing reduces the quadratic cost and parameter count by selecting a subset of experts per token [S2].\n\n**Rotary positional encodings (RoPE)**  \n- Injects position information by rotating query and key vectors within the attention mechanism [S9].  \n- Scaling the rotation can extend the model's context length beyond the training limit [S9].  \n- Unlike absolute or relative position biases, RoPE modifies the query/key vectors directly, making the position encoding intrinsic to the attention computation.\n\nIn short, MoE routing changes *which* feed-forward sub\u2011layers are activated per token, reducing compute while retaining capacity; rotary encodings change *how* positional information is supplied to the attention layers, enabling length generalisation and a different form of positional bias.", "sources": [{"alias": "S1", "external_id": "ml-03", "tier": "peer_reviewed"}, {"alias": "S2", "external_id": "ml-01", "tier": "peer_reviewed"}, {"alias": "S3", "external_id": "ag-11", "tier": "lab_blog"}, {"alias": "S4", "external_id": "ml-05", "tier": "lab_blog"}, {"alias": "S5", "external_id": "af-01", "tier": "peer_reviewed"}, {"alias": "S6", "external_id": "ag-05", "tier": "peer_reviewed"}, {"alias": "S7", "external_id": "ag-14", "tier": "peer_reviewed"}, {"alias": "S8", "external_id": "ag-18", "tier": "lab_blog"}, {"alias": "S9", "external_id": "ml-04", "tier": "vetted_preprint"}, {"alias": "S10", "external_id": "af-04", "tier": "vetted_preprint"}, {"alias": "S11", "external_id": "ag-06", "tier": "lab_blog"}], "tools": ["search_corpus", "search_corpus", "search_corpus"], "tokens": 7197, "provider_error": false}
{"question_id": "q16", "model": "nvidia/nemotron-3.5-lightning:free", "set_version": 1, "answer_text": "Text watermarking and attacking an image watermark differ in medium, embedding method, and adversarial goal:\n\n- **Text watermarking** [S1] embeds a secret\u2011key\u2011driven bias into the token\u2011generation process of a language model. Later, a detector can recover the secret signal to prove the text was machine\u2011generated, providing provenance tracing.\n\n- **Attacking an image watermark** [S4] treats the watermark as a vulnerability: an adversary perturbs a generated image (e.g., through pixel\u2011level noise) until the watermark detector fails to flag it. Robustness of the image watermark is measured against common image transformations such as compression and cropping.\n\nIn short, text watermarking **embeds** a detectable bias for later verification, while attacking an image watermark **evades** that detection, with distinct robustness considerations for each modality.", "sources": [{"alias": "S1", "external_id": "af-02", "tier": "vetted_preprint"}, {"alias": "S2", "external_id": "af-01", "tier": "peer_reviewed"}, {"alias": "S3", "external_id": "af-03", "tier": "peer_reviewed"}, {"alias": "S4", "external_id": "af-05", "tier": "lab_blog"}, {"alias": "S5", "external_id": "af-06", "tier": "peer_reviewed"}, {"alias": "S6", "external_id": "ag-14", "tier": "peer_reviewed"}, {"alias": "S7", "external_id": "dec-03", "tier": "peer_reviewed"}, {"alias": "S8", "external_id": "dc-02", "tier": "vetted_preprint"}], "tools": ["search_corpus", "get_item", "get_item"], "tokens": 7233, "provider_error": false}
